cubie-a7a-kmods provenance
==========================

Generated by fedora/kmods/import.py from two trees:

  series: Linux a74306e2e676f9775457366fc047a660fbf02f26 with the Cubie A7A series applied
          (the board's Linux patch series, 53 patches), the eight A733 CCU patches replaced by
          their v6 posting (2026-10-09, msgid 20261009-a733-clk-v6-1-ae8178fce7e8@pigmoral.tech:
          R-CCU bus clock R_TWD dropped (secure-only register; R-CCU clock IDs after 8
          shift by one), CLK_MBUS_NAND renamed CLK_MBUS_NAND0, ahb-store parent of the
          storage bus gates, mbus-store critical). Regenerated 2026-10-15.
  fedora: linux-7.2.10 + patch-7.2-redhat.patch from kernel-7.2.10-200.fc44.src.rpm
          (Fedora's signed SRPM; used only for kernel-internal headers).
          SRPM SHA256 81c449bfcee70cf5016b2d1500f4c352d230f2f9c393a41942e1e56bca4230f8.
          Compared all26 imported headers to7.2.8:25 byte-identical; hwif.h
          changes only one function-parameter name, with no ABI change.

  bus master gates (2026-11-11): ccu/ccu-sun60i-a733.c carries two local
  changes not in the series: the 35 gates in CCU registers 0x5c0, 0x5e0 and
  0x5e4 keep a software copy of each register so a write to one gate cannot
  clear another master's gate (their readback follows the master's power
  domain). ahb-gpu0/mbus-gpu0 were critical as in the vendor driver from
  2026-11-11 (patch 0002); since 2026-11-12 (GPU power on demand) they are
  ordinary gates that the PCK-600 provider holds while GPU_TOP is on (clock
  names gpu-ahb/gpu-mbus on its node, binding stamp 20). Evidence and the
  same change for the Linux tree: fedora/kmods/a733-master-gates/.

  pll-npu (2026-11-11): ccu/ccu-sun60i-a733.c gives PLL_NPU the vendor's N
  range (53-105) and no input divider, and clears its bit 1 in probe, so
  492 MHz is N=82, M=4 (VCO 1968 MHz) instead of N=41 with bit 1 set. Not in
  the series; see fedora/kmods/a733-vipcore/SPEED.md.
  fedora 7.3 (2026-11-10): stmmac.h, hwif.h and dwxgmac2.h replaced by the
          files of linux-7.3.3 from kernel-7.3.3-300.fc45.src.rpm (SRPM SHA256
          7f1a1de7f12d1dd9a1560ad6a9b0a59e0d75698c489671ba2297c1d27f7ca4e8).
          The other 23 imported headers, sun6i-dma.c, dwmac-sun55i.c,
          sunxi_sid.c and sun55i-pck600.c are byte-identical in 7.2.10 and
          7.3.3; stock sun8i_thermal.c only drops regmap fast_io (kept here).
          pcie-sun60i-a733.c: irq_domain_create_linear (7.3 removed
          irq_domain_add_linear).

Per-file origin and the sha256 of each origin file are in SOURCES.sha256.
All code is GPL-2.0-only (see the SPDX line of each file) and keeps its
